A||||8||V8Fiero||Tires for 16" rims?||||5||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||04-26-2001||09:39 PM||||ok. <P>I did search on this topic. Wow!! I think I confused myself more than trying to find an answer.<P>Here what I have:<BR>16 x 7.5 38mm offset<BR> <BR>I test fit them and there is about a half an inch (maybe a hair more) between the rim and strut. I need a tire that is just about flush with the rim.<BR>Any suggestions?<P>thanks<BR>Scott||||reg||5
Z||000001||85Josh||04-26-2001||09:49 PM||||A 195 section width is very close to 7.5". A 205 is still going to allow about a quarter inch clearance, and probably look better. If your tire is flush with the rim, curbside parking becomes dangerous to your rims! Other people, with more experience in this, will probably chime in.<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||Wannabe||04-26-2001||10:12 PM||||225-50 should work well. I had this size on 16x7's with 42mm offset and there was no problem. This tire is also the same diameter as the stock 215-60-15.||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Fiero||04-27-2001||12:00 AM||||After some more searching the archives it seems that Im kindof leaning towards 205/55/16. How do you guys/gals think those would work?<BR>Anyone running that size on your rims? <P>Scott||||reg||6
Z||000004||Philphine||04-27-2001||01:34 AM||||i have two fieros with 16x7.5 rims. one has 225/50-16's in front and 255/50-16's in back. the other has 225/40-16's all around. the 255's require coilovers but i like the look. the 225/40's look too small (to me). i plan to end up with 225/45-16's all around or maybe 245/45-16's in the rear.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||04-27-2001||02:10 AM||||Im running 225/50ZR16's on the Formula. Its a nice size tire..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">    </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
Z||000006||1FST2M6||04-27-2001||03:52 PM||||i'm with Haze and wannabe||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||04-27-2001||08:12 PM||||I have 205 50ZR16 front and 225 50R16 rear because they were on the rims.  The 225's are a nice size...car should be lowered but the roads are too bad here!<P>Gary||||reg||14
Z||000008||Songman||04-27-2001||09:46 PM||||I'm running 225/50s on one of my 88s, but they are 15s... Plenty of room in the back and all around.. and they do look very cool!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
